MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_001: Diego Oro. I must speak with you.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_002: Why? Are you here to punish me?
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_003: No. I wanted you to know that your family is in\ngood health.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_004: The Har Hali, under my command, have taken refuge\nin Saramis.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_005: Your parents are among them. I thought you might\nhave been worried.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_006: Not my business. I doubt they still think of me as a\nson after I fled from the ritual. Especially Father.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_007: Oro did say that. But I think he had his reasons.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_008: His way of trying to protect Mother, I guess.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_009: Or else she'd be ostracized for giving birth to\na deserter.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_010: You knew?
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_011: Everyone knows a husband will look after his wife.\nIf that's all you had to say, we're done here.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_012: Wait, Diego. I'm not asking you to come back to us.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_013: But won't you consider visiting so your parents can\nsee your face again?
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_014: I'll be there to ensure no one blames you. Please...
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_015: Why would you do that for me? My family\nwasn't special.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_016: Or have you convinced yourself this is a chief's duty?\nBecause I don't care about that.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_017: No. I'm doing this because...I want to.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_018: Oh yeah? I don't remember my family being close\nto you.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_019: I want to do the right thing. That's all.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_020: Before, I never questioned the rites and ceremonies\nof the Har Hali.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_021: I envied you when you were chosen to be an\nassassin. It seemed like a great honor.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_022: And like everyone else, when I heard you ran away,\nI thought you were a coward.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_023: O-oh...
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_024: But then I saw Bahr Vahn go mad. I became acting\nchief of the Har Hali.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_025: I met the queen of Saramis and breathed in the fresh\nair outside our forest. I'm a different person now.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_026: And I know it would bring your parents joy to see\ntheir son alive.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_027: It would show them it was good that you weren't\nsacrificed to Balor.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_028: The other chosen assassins from that day are dead.\nOnly you are left, Diego.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_029: This won't achieve anything. It's too late.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_030: Even if you reunite me with my parents, it won't\nbring any of us comfort.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_031: You're probably right.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_032: I have no reason to visit my parents. But I'll\nthink about what you said.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_033: And if I ever change my mind...I'll let you know.
MID_SE_Die_Nuz_C_034: Ah... Alright. That's the most I can ask.